1
00:00:01,793 --> 00:00:03,086
<i>You know what, Caloy?</i>

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:05,755
<i>You'll be back behind bars</i>
<i>if that happens.</i>

3
00:00:05,839 --> 00:00:07,215
<i>I know.</i>

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:10,719
<i>Dino has a point.</i>

5
00:00:11,594 --> 00:00:13,096
<i>I'll get in trouble</i>

6
00:00:13,179 --> 00:00:16,599
<i>if I shoot that bastard</i>
<i>right in front of his bar.</i>

7
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:18,893
<i>Look at that. You know it too.</i>

8
00:00:19,686 --> 00:00:22,647
<i>That's why you should turn over a new leaf</i>
<i>and stop that already.</i>

9
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:28,069
<i>I could just make it</i>
<i>look like an accident.</i>

10
00:00:30,405 --> 00:00:32,699
<i>Where are our IDs and passports?</i>

11
00:00:32,782 --> 00:00:34,325
<i>Your ID isn't ready yet.</i>

12
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:36,828
<i>What's taking so long? I can pay you.</i>

13
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:38,163
<i>I'll get money from my son.</i>

14
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:40,957
<i>That's if</i>

15
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:42,459
<i>he can still lend you some.</i>

16
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:47,255
<i>What do you mean?</i>

17
00:00:50,842 --> 00:00:51,885
<i>Where's Caloy?</i>

18
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:59,517
<i>We will be filing an</i>
<i>Affidavit of Desistance</i>

19
00:00:59,601 --> 00:01:02,187
<i>with the Office of the Prosecutor</i>
<i>handling your case.</i>

20
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:04,355
<i>Ah…</i>

21
00:01:04,439 --> 00:01:05,690
<i>Desistance?</i>

22
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:09,944
<i>Ms. Cariño has already withdrawn</i>
<i>the charges against you.</i>

23
00:01:11,404 --> 00:01:12,530
[CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY]

24
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:14,240
<i>Billy.</i>

25
00:01:14,324 --> 00:01:16,034
<i>Billy, thank you so much.</i>

26
00:01:16,117 --> 00:01:18,161
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

27
00:01:18,244 --> 00:01:20,955
<i>What about-- what about my mother?</i>

28
00:01:21,039 --> 00:01:25,001
<i>Will you withdraw the charges</i>
<i>against her too?</i>

29
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:27,378
<i>If you were in my position,</i>

30
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:33,593
<i>and your family had almost died</i>
<i>because of someone…</i>

31
00:01:36,429 --> 00:01:38,598
<i>would you really let her walk free?</i>

32
00:01:42,435 --> 00:01:43,436
<i>Sorry.</i>

33
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:47,023
[STUTTERS] <i>You're right, Billy.</i>

34
00:01:47,106 --> 00:01:49,109
[PRECIOUS]<i> Your daughter</i>
<i>couldn't say no to you.</i>

35
00:01:49,692 --> 00:01:51,194
<i>That's how much she loves you.</i>

36
00:01:51,277 --> 00:01:53,238
<i>When is Bea getting out?</i>

37
00:01:53,321 --> 00:01:56,533
<i>Until an official</i>
<i>court dismissal order is issued,</i>

38
00:01:57,992 --> 00:01:59,369
<i>she isn't allowed out.</i>

39
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:02,038
<i>Do you think Bea has truly changed?</i>

40
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:04,165
<i>She made a promise to me.</i>

41
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:06,334
<i>Do you believe her?</i>

42
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:09,003
<i>I have to.</i>

43
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:12,590
<i>Dude.</i>

44
00:02:13,091 --> 00:02:14,175
<i>Just relax.</i>

45
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:15,760
<i>Okay?</i>

46
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:17,178
<i>You're just stressed out.</i>

47
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:19,389
<i>Jordan, of course I'm stressed!</i>

48
00:02:19,472 --> 00:02:22,016
<i>People's livelihoods are at stake here.</i>

49
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:26,104
<i>And you want me to do what?</i>
<i>Go to your bar to chill?</i>

50
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:33,611
<i>Shit.</i>

51
00:02:37,073 --> 00:02:38,074
<i>Sorry, dude.</i>

52
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,200
<i>Sorry, sorry.</i>

53
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:43,204
<i>Dude.</i>

54
00:02:43,288 --> 00:02:46,916
<i>I know you don't want to</i>
<i>drop the case against Bea.</i>

55
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,084
<i>Okay?</i>

56
00:02:52,171 --> 00:02:57,760
<i>If I don't give Dad what he's asking for,</i>
<i>and something happens to him,</i>

57
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:01,931
<i>I'll carry that guilt</i>
<i>for the rest of my life.</i>

58
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:04,225
<i>Can I make a suggestion?</i>

59
00:03:06,019 --> 00:03:07,186
<i>Go home.</i>

60
00:03:07,812 --> 00:03:09,898
<i>- Get some rest.</i>
<i>- Okay.</i>

61
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:12,650
[TIRES SCREECH]

62
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:14,110
[ENGINE REVVING]

63
00:03:14,193 --> 00:03:17,405
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

64
00:03:19,699 --> 00:03:20,992
[TIRES SCREECHING]

65
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:25,705
[TIRES SCREECHING]

66
00:03:25,788 --> 00:03:26,873
[GRUNTS]

67
00:03:27,457 --> 00:03:28,374
[GRUNTS]

68
00:03:30,627 --> 00:03:31,628
Ugh!

69
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:33,713
- Boss!
- [DINO GROANS]

70
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:35,632
I almost had him!

71
00:03:35,715 --> 00:03:37,926
[JORDAN BREATHING HEAVILY]

72
00:03:38,009 --> 00:03:40,678
[DINO BREATHING HEAVILY]

73
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:43,348
Dad?

74
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:46,601
Be careful, Jordan.

75
00:03:46,684 --> 00:03:48,436
Watch out for Caloy.

76
00:03:48,519 --> 00:03:53,107
Carlos-- Carlos Toledo wants to kill you.

77
00:03:53,191 --> 00:03:55,985
All right? Watch out for Carlos Toledo.

78
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:57,320
Be careful!

79
00:04:05,662 --> 00:04:06,663
Boss.

80
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:08,289
Are you okay?

81
00:04:12,752 --> 00:04:19,717
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

82
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:24,657
<i>A massive manhunt is underway</i>
<i>for the fugitives who escaped from prison.</i>

83
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:31,539
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

84
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:33,082
You're getting famous.

85
00:05:36,127 --> 00:05:38,337
I have to warn Jordan.

86
00:05:40,882 --> 00:05:42,633
You're acting like a hero.

87
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:44,010
Are you getting anything in return?

88
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:46,512
What?

89
00:05:47,722 --> 00:05:50,308
Wait. What are you doing?
Where are you going?!

90
00:05:50,933 --> 00:05:52,101
Dino!

91
00:05:55,063 --> 00:05:58,816
Carlos Toledo and Dino Valentin
were among those who escaped.

92
00:06:00,276 --> 00:06:01,944
Sir, with all due respect,

93
00:06:02,028 --> 00:06:03,529
why didn't you tell us before?

94
00:06:03,613 --> 00:06:07,575
You know Jordan was one of the people
who got Caloy jailed.

95
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:10,828
We already have leads
on their whereabouts.

96
00:06:10,912 --> 00:06:11,996
Leads?

97
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:16,084
That means you're still just
hoping to catch them,

98
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:19,087
so you're only informing us now that
those bastards have escaped.

99
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:21,923
My boss almost got into an accident!

100
00:06:22,006 --> 00:06:23,758
[POLICE] Don't worry, sir.

101
00:06:23,841 --> 00:06:27,720
We won't stop searching
for Toledo and for your father.

102
00:06:28,846 --> 00:06:30,348
- [SLAMS TABLE]
- Well, obviously.

103
00:06:30,431 --> 00:06:33,935
Obviously, sir,
you shouldn't stop searching.

104
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,938
But I hope you can protect my friend too.

105
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:47,490
Dad saved my life?

106
00:06:47,573 --> 00:06:53,955
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

107
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,253
I'll leave that to you.

108
00:07:01,379 --> 00:07:02,713
I have to be here.

109
00:07:02,797 --> 00:07:04,298
But, boss,

110
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:07,176
aren't you Caloy's only target?

111
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:09,428
I hope it is just me.

112
00:07:10,596 --> 00:07:13,141
Uh, boss, have you warned Billy?

113
00:07:13,224 --> 00:07:14,559
[JORDAN SIGHS]

114
00:07:15,393 --> 00:07:17,228
Billy's already got too many problems.

115
00:07:17,812 --> 00:07:20,231
[JORDAN] <i>She doesn't need</i>
<i>to know about Caloy for now.</i>

116
00:07:21,774 --> 00:07:23,651
I just need to make sure she's safe.

117
00:07:24,694 --> 00:07:27,530
I also requested police surveillance

118
00:07:28,072 --> 00:07:29,240
around their area.

119
00:07:29,824 --> 00:07:32,535
- Are the cops there?
- Not yet.

120
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:34,537
But they'll arrive soon.

121
00:07:35,413 --> 00:07:37,623
I just told them to be discreet for now.

122
00:07:38,374 --> 00:07:39,625
I don't want Billy to panic.

123
00:07:43,004 --> 00:07:45,631
All right, I have to go now. She's here.

124
00:07:46,215 --> 00:07:47,258
Bye.

125
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:53,639
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

126
00:07:53,723 --> 00:07:54,932
So?

127
00:07:55,016 --> 00:07:56,851
Why are you here?

128
00:07:57,518 --> 00:08:00,521
Dude, I'm fine. You don't
have to check on me.

129
00:08:01,147 --> 00:08:03,024
I know it's busy at the bar right now.

130
00:08:04,609 --> 00:08:05,651
That's the thing, dude.

131
00:08:06,402 --> 00:08:09,071
It's too busy right now. Too much noise.

132
00:08:09,155 --> 00:08:12,492
I want to be somewhere quiet.

133
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:14,911
I'm just getting stressed there.

134
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:17,455
You're stressed?

135
00:08:18,039 --> 00:08:19,040
[JORDAN EXHALES]

136
00:08:19,665 --> 00:08:20,583
I'm fine.

137
00:08:20,666 --> 00:08:22,710
Do you have a problem too?

138
00:08:22,793 --> 00:08:25,129
Dude, please don't worry about me.

139
00:08:25,213 --> 00:08:26,339
Okay?

140
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:28,841
Right now, I just want
to be here with you.

141
00:08:28,925 --> 00:08:30,593
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

142
00:08:30,676 --> 00:08:31,594
With me?

143
00:08:32,929 --> 00:08:35,723
Maybe I can… stay here for now?

144
00:08:36,682 --> 00:08:37,808
Just for tonight.

145
00:08:39,810 --> 00:08:42,813
Unless I'm bothering you?

146
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:46,692
I'll sleep on the couch.

147
00:08:47,443 --> 00:08:48,819
- There?
- Yes!

148
00:08:48,903 --> 00:08:50,321
I'll be fine.

149
00:08:52,281 --> 00:08:55,243
Just like when we were kids!
Remember our sleepovers?

150
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:57,662
I'll be fine.

151
00:08:59,539 --> 00:09:00,373
Okay.

152
00:09:03,167 --> 00:09:04,335
I'll get you a pillow.

153
00:09:08,256 --> 00:09:09,590
[SIGHS]

154
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:14,845
[WILFRED GROANING]

155
00:09:14,929 --> 00:09:16,556
Do you really not know where Caloy is?

156
00:09:16,639 --> 00:09:18,224
Believe me. Believe me.

157
00:09:18,307 --> 00:09:20,351
Believe me, Dino. I really don't know!

158
00:09:20,434 --> 00:09:22,061
If I learn that you're lying to me,

159
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:23,145
you're dead.

160
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:24,981
[CRYING] Yes! Yes!

161
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:26,607
You already know how to contact me.

162
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:29,819
If you hear anything about Caloy,
let me know right away.

163
00:09:29,902 --> 00:09:31,362
- Do you understand?
- Yes, yes!

164
00:09:31,445 --> 00:09:34,615
[WILFRED BREATHING HEAVILY]

165
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:42,456
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

166
00:09:43,666 --> 00:09:44,667
[PASSPORT THUDS]

167
00:09:44,750 --> 00:09:50,923
[WILFRED BREATHING HEAVILY]

168
00:09:55,094 --> 00:10:00,266
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

169
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:02,977
Thank you.

170
00:10:04,478 --> 00:10:07,523
[WILFRED BREATHING HEAVILY]

171
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:11,652
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

172
00:10:11,736 --> 00:10:14,405
[PRECIOUS] Maybe you should
call his friends.

173
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:18,701
I already talked to Robbie and Rain.

174
00:10:18,784 --> 00:10:22,747
They said he's probably stressed
because of the bar.

175
00:10:23,456 --> 00:10:25,708
It could also be about Grandpa Jude.

176
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:27,168
See?

177
00:10:27,251 --> 00:10:30,671
He's going through a lot,
but you know what's important?

178
00:10:30,755 --> 00:10:31,922
Going through it together.

179
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:35,217
[BILLY] That's the thing, Auntie.

180
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:40,014
Work has been stressing me out lately.

181
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:43,100
And I took out my anger on him.

182
00:10:44,018 --> 00:10:46,604
Ah, so you did go through it together.

183
00:10:46,687 --> 00:10:48,856
Just in a different way.

184
00:10:51,067 --> 00:10:56,322
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

185
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:14,090
[TIRES SCREECHING]

186
00:11:16,467 --> 00:11:18,052
- [JORDAN GRUNTS]
- Jordan!

187
00:11:18,135 --> 00:11:19,178
What's happening?!

188
00:11:19,261 --> 00:11:20,346
Relax!

189
00:11:20,846 --> 00:11:22,556
- Relax, okay?
- Oh my God.

190
00:11:23,224 --> 00:11:25,101
Dude, I'm sorry.

191
00:11:27,311 --> 00:11:29,772
Are you okay? Huh?

192
00:11:29,855 --> 00:11:33,442
If you have a problem,
you can talk to me, okay?

193
00:11:34,235 --> 00:11:35,903
You look more stressed than me.

194
00:11:36,612 --> 00:11:38,948
Dude, I'm fine.

195
00:11:41,659 --> 00:11:42,701
Thank you.

196
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:45,955
For letting me stay tonight.

197
00:11:49,166 --> 00:11:51,252
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

198
00:11:51,335 --> 00:11:52,920
Get some rest. Good night.

199
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:04,306
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

200
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:17,528
[MUSIC BECOMES PENSIVE]

201
00:12:17,611 --> 00:12:18,737
POLICE

202
00:12:30,207 --> 00:12:31,584
[MUSIC FADES]

203
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:37,923
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:12:53,147 --> 00:12:54,607
[CALOY GRUNTS]

205
00:12:54,690 --> 00:12:55,816
<i>Let's go!</i>

206
00:12:58,235 --> 00:13:00,154
<i>Bastards!</i>
[GASPING]

207
00:13:03,657 --> 00:13:05,451
<i>Help! Help! Hold on!</i>

208
00:13:05,534 --> 00:13:07,620
<i>Take me to the hospital! It hurts!</i>

209
00:13:07,703 --> 00:13:09,288
[HORN HONKING]

210
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:10,873
<i>Sir, help me, please.</i>

211
00:13:12,291 --> 00:13:14,585
[CALOY GRUNTING]

212
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:16,712
<i>Oh, there's blood!</i>

213
00:13:16,795 --> 00:13:19,298
<i>Sir? Hey! Are you okay?</i>

214
00:13:19,381 --> 00:13:20,591
<i>Help! Help!</i>

215
00:13:20,674 --> 00:13:22,176
<i>Oh! That looks pretty deep.</i>

216
00:13:22,259 --> 00:13:24,470
<i>What, are you all deaf? Help!</i>

217
00:13:24,553 --> 00:13:25,679
<i>Tricycle!</i>

218
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:27,348
<i>What happened to you?</i>

219
00:13:27,431 --> 00:13:29,308
<i>Oh my God!</i>
<i>Get in!</i>

220
00:13:29,391 --> 00:13:30,809
<i>To the nearest hospital, please!</i>

221
00:13:30,893 --> 00:13:31,936
<i>Let's go, hurry!</i>

222
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:36,565
<i>My parents disowned me.</i>

223
00:13:40,277 --> 00:13:42,530
<i>But you, someone I'm not even related to…</i>

224
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:46,200
<i>have always been by my side.</i>

225
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:51,080
<i>Caloy, we're the same, aren't we?</i>

226
00:13:51,789 --> 00:13:53,707
<i>Our parents both abandoned us.</i>

227
00:13:56,669 --> 00:13:59,922
<i>That's why we're all we've got.</i>

228
00:14:01,006 --> 00:14:03,008
<i>So I hope you understand</i>

229
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:07,096
<i>why we need to keep our distance for now.</i>

230
00:14:07,846 --> 00:14:09,265
<i>It's for our own good.</i>

231
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:12,309
<i>We have to be even more careful.</i>

232
00:14:12,935 --> 00:14:14,103
<i>Anything for you.</i>

233
00:14:14,645 --> 00:14:15,771
<i>- Stop!</i>
<i>- I need to pee.</i>

234
00:14:15,854 --> 00:14:17,773
<i>You need to go home.</i>

235
00:14:17,856 --> 00:14:19,775
<i>Billy might just be around.</i>

236
00:14:19,859 --> 00:14:22,361
<i>What if she finds out</i>
<i>we're working together?</i>

237
00:14:23,571 --> 00:14:25,281
<i>You're so stubborn, Caloy.</i>

238
00:14:25,364 --> 00:14:27,825
<i>I've told you so many times</i>
<i>that we shouldn't meet.</i>

239
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:29,118
<i>But you won't listen!</i>

240
00:14:29,201 --> 00:14:31,036
<i>Starting today, we really shouldn't meet!</i>

241
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:33,998
<i>I can't do that.</i>

242
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:36,250
<i>You know I can't leave you alone.</i>

243
00:14:36,333 --> 00:14:37,543
<i>- Abi…</i>
<i>- You're such a flirt!</i>

244
00:14:37,626 --> 00:14:39,920
<i>We're partners, right?</i>
<i>We should stick together.</i>

245
00:14:40,796 --> 00:14:43,173
<i>C'mon, you don't need to play hard to get.</i>

246
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:46,635
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

247
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:48,679
<i>Seriously, Caloy?!</i>
<i>I don't have time for your nonsense.</i>

248
00:14:48,762 --> 00:14:50,514
<i>- What are you doing here?</i>
<i>- Don't you appreciate me?</i>

249
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:51,473
<i>Hurry up!</i>

250
00:14:51,557 --> 00:14:53,183
<i>So you finally admit</i>
<i>you've forgotten about me.</i>

251
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:55,769
<i>Caloy, what is your problem?!</i>
<i>What are you talking about?!</i>

252
00:14:55,853 --> 00:14:57,021
<i>Seriously?!</i>

253
00:14:57,104 --> 00:14:59,064
<i>Can't you see I'm working?</i>

254
00:14:59,148 --> 00:15:00,399
<i>You're starting to sound like my mom,</i>

255
00:15:00,482 --> 00:15:02,860
<i>always asking where I'm going</i>
<i>and what I'm doing!</i>

256
00:15:02,943 --> 00:15:06,030
<i>I wouldn't even be surprised</i>
<i>if she showed up here and caused a scene.</i>

257
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:07,197
<i>That will totally ruin my plan.</i>

258
00:15:07,281 --> 00:15:08,240
<i>Just like you!</i>

259
00:15:08,324 --> 00:15:09,533
<i>What, are you my mother now?!</i>

260
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:10,534
<i>No!</i>

261
00:15:11,243 --> 00:15:12,786
<i>Then why are you here?!</i>

262
00:15:15,831 --> 00:15:17,416
<i>So what am I to you, anyway?</i>

263
00:15:19,084 --> 00:15:21,795
<i>- Because I love you.</i>
<i>- Cut it out!</i>

264
00:15:24,423 --> 00:15:25,466
<i>Are you okay?</i>

265
00:15:29,929 --> 00:15:31,764
[SOBBING, SNIFFLING]

266
00:15:41,023 --> 00:15:47,905
[SOBBING]

267
00:15:52,076 --> 00:15:53,369
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

268
00:15:57,623 --> 00:16:03,796
[DARK MUSIC SWELLS]

269
00:16:05,923 --> 00:16:07,174
[MUSIC STOPS]

270
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:17,601
- [CHUCKLING]
- Her? Getting out?

271
00:16:18,352 --> 00:16:19,687
Why are you all staring at me?

272
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:22,272
Hmm, I know.
[SCOFFS]

273
00:16:22,940 --> 00:16:24,900
You're all going to miss me!

274
00:16:26,110 --> 00:16:27,653
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

275
00:16:27,736 --> 00:16:31,031
Why? Are you sure that
you'll be able to get out?

276
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:32,950
Absolutely.

277
00:16:33,492 --> 00:16:35,035
That's for sure.

278
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:36,745
So if I were you,

279
00:16:37,246 --> 00:16:39,581
I'd behave myself so I could get out too.

280
00:16:39,665 --> 00:16:42,292
[CHUCKLES] This delusional bitch
is hilarious.

281
00:16:42,376 --> 00:16:44,962
She probably won't even make it past the
gate before she comes crawling back.

282
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:46,088
[LAUGHTER]

283
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:51,760
Where are you going?
To a mental institution as well?

284
00:16:52,928 --> 00:16:55,347
With your crazy mother?

285
00:16:56,432 --> 00:16:58,100
- What?!
- Who are you calling crazy?

286
00:16:58,183 --> 00:17:00,477
Why did they even bother
taking her to the hospital?

287
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:02,354
- She's a lost cause!
- Yeah.

288
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:04,606
- Just like you!
- A lost cause?

289
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:06,108
Let's see who's really the lost cause!

290
00:17:06,191 --> 00:17:12,114
- [BLOW LANDS]
- [OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

291
00:17:12,197 --> 00:17:13,699
[INMATE] Somebody get help!

292
00:17:14,283 --> 00:17:16,618
- Ahh!
- Witch!

293
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:18,579
- You bitch!
- [BLOW LANDS]

294
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:21,373
[OVERLAPPING CLAMOR]

295
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:22,875
[GUARD WHISTLE BLOWS]

296
00:17:22,958 --> 00:17:27,588
[BLOWS LANDING]

297
00:17:32,009 --> 00:17:34,178
[PRISON GUARD]
Ma'am? Ma'am?

298
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:35,971
Wake up, ma'am. Ma'am?

299
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:42,102
[SIREN WAILING]

300
00:17:42,186 --> 00:17:49,151
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

301
00:18:10,422 --> 00:18:11,340
<i>Jordan?</i>

302
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:18,180
<i>What are you doing here?</i>

303
00:18:22,476 --> 00:18:24,311
<i>I'm here to ask for your forgiveness.</i>

304
00:18:26,146 --> 00:18:27,231
<i>I've changed.</i>

305
00:18:27,898 --> 00:18:28,941
<i>I've changed, son.</i>

306
00:18:30,109 --> 00:18:31,485
<i>Did you break out?</i>

307
00:18:31,568 --> 00:18:32,945
<i>Is that what a changed person does?</i>

308
00:18:33,028 --> 00:18:35,656
<i>You even escaped with</i>
<i>Caloy Toledo.</i>

309
00:18:36,615 --> 00:18:37,991
<i>I'm worried about you.</i>

310
00:18:38,075 --> 00:18:41,620
<i>I'm sure he'll come after you.</i>

311
00:18:41,703 --> 00:18:42,913
<i>He'll come back for you.</i>

312
00:18:43,747 --> 00:18:44,915
<i>He…</i>

313
00:18:45,749 --> 00:18:47,751
<i>He became my friend</i>
<i>while we were inside.</i>

314
00:18:47,835 --> 00:18:49,670
<i>But I didn't know</i>
<i>you two were enemies.</i>

315
00:18:49,753 --> 00:18:51,755
<i>When I found out he was planning</i>
<i>to do something to you,</i>

316
00:18:51,839 --> 00:18:52,881
<i>I followed him.</i>

317
00:18:53,632 --> 00:18:56,969
<i>I know I've hurt you</i>
<i>and your mom.</i>

318
00:18:57,052 --> 00:18:59,596
<i>That's why I'm here now.</i>
<i>To make amends.</i>

319
00:19:02,057 --> 00:19:04,143
<i>She suffered a head trauma.</i>

320
00:19:04,226 --> 00:19:07,396
<i>However, we didn't find</i>
<i>any internal bleeding.</i>

321
00:19:07,479 --> 00:19:09,731
<i>But she needs to be</i>
<i>under observation</i>

322
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:12,734
<i>for at least another 24 hours.</i>

323
00:19:12,818 --> 00:19:14,945
<i>It's dangerous for you</i>
<i>to stay here, Caloy.</i>

324
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:16,613
<i>And for me too. So just leave.</i>

325
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:18,699
<i>It'll only be dangerous</i>
<i>if you snitch on me.</i>

326
00:19:18,782 --> 00:19:21,577
<i>I'm sure Dino won't leave me alone.</i>

327
00:19:21,660 --> 00:19:24,079
<i>He won't come after you.</i>
<i>Don't be a coward.</i>

328
00:19:24,163 --> 00:19:25,581
<i>I can feel it.</i>

329
00:19:27,124 --> 00:19:29,543
<i>He doesn't believe that you're gone.</i>

330
00:19:29,626 --> 00:19:31,795
<i>What if he gives the police a tip?</i>

331
00:19:32,379 --> 00:19:34,298
<i>So please, I'm begging you,</i>
<i>get out of here.</i>

332
00:19:35,924 --> 00:19:37,843
<i>Hey. Put that away.</i>

333
00:19:38,510 --> 00:19:41,180
<i>What you're planning is dangerous.</i>

334
00:19:42,764 --> 00:19:46,059
<i>I don't want to call the police</i>
<i>if Caloy isn't even here.</i>

335
00:19:46,810 --> 00:19:48,061
<i>We'll find out.</i>

336
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:53,525
<i>And once we're sure</i>
<i>he's still here,</i>

337
00:19:55,068 --> 00:19:56,361
<i>promise me</i>

338
00:19:57,529 --> 00:19:59,531
<i>you'll turn yourself in</i>
<i>to the police.</i>

339
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:06,121
<i>Caloy!</i>

340
00:20:10,792 --> 00:20:15,130
[BLOWS LANDING]

341
00:20:17,507 --> 00:20:21,178
All right!
[CALOY GRUNTS]

342
00:20:22,804 --> 00:20:24,473
<i>I'll be back, okay? I'll be quick.</i>

343
00:20:24,556 --> 00:20:25,682
<i>Wait.</i>

344
00:20:29,061 --> 00:20:31,355
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

345
00:20:36,652 --> 00:20:38,528
<i>That necklace belonged</i>
<i>to my mom.</i>

346
00:20:40,656 --> 00:20:42,908
<i>This is mine.</i>
<i>Your father gave it to me.</i>

347
00:20:43,617 --> 00:20:50,540
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]
